# Line endings, decided here rather than per machine.
#
# Every text file in this repository is stored and checked out with Unix line endings. This is not a
# style preference. Git Bash strips a carriage return transparently in grep, sed and awk while a real
# Linux shell does not, so a file that picks up Windows line endings passes the tier 1 gate from Git
# Bash and fails it from WSL and inside every container. That happened: three checks reported eight
# failures under WSL against a tree that Git Bash called clean, and the cause was invisible in every
# diff, because a carriage return has no width.
#
# Without this file the outcome depends on each clone's core.autocrlf setting, which is a local
# preference no reviewer can see.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary content, so Git never inspects or rewrites it. text=auto already detects these, and naming
# them is what makes the intent explicit rather than inferred.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.knsv binary
